  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A small spherical body of radius $r$ and density p moves with the terminal velocity $v$ in a fluid of coefficient of viscosity $\\eta$ and density $\\bar{\\sigma}$. What will be the net force on the body?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4lXcF",
      "text": "$\\frac{4 \\pi}{3} r^{3}(p-\\sigma) g$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ru4d9",
      "text": "$6 \\pi \\eta rv$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Uhonx",
      "text": "Zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "C0Xph",
      "text": "Infinity",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When the spherical body falls with constant velocity, i.e. terminal velocity then the net force becomes zero, i.e the weight of body is equal to the buoyancy force. Hence, $F_{\\text {net }}=0$",
    "image": null
  },
